WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:02.469
-Getting a standing --
-That's not normal?

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.536
-That's not normal.
No, that's not normal.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:05.037
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:07.039
That's for you.

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.074
Come on.
-I thought you...

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:10.309
I thought you might have, like,
goosed the seats or something.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:12.745
-No, I didn't goose the seats.
No.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.014
They love you, bud.
-Oh, that's very sweet.

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.917
-That's got to feel good
coming from a comedian

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:21.487
who used to work in the theater
and work in front of a crowd.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.856
-Yeah, and then to actually see
an actual crowd again, yeah.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.292
-Don't you miss that?
-I do, I do, yeah.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.227
-Was your first taste
of an audience

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.830
when you did ComedySportz?

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.899
-Yes, it was. Yeah.
Yeah, ComedySportz.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.200
With a "Z."

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.769
With a "Z," 'cause it's
a comedy show, yeah.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:37.704
-Of course. I have a photo here.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.338
That's why --
I wanted to show you.

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:42.375
This is you...
-Yeah, that's me there.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.444
-...at ComedySportz.
-Yeah, that's me right there.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.712
-Now --

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.047
-That's my buddy
Billy right there, yeah.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.948
-Yeah, and the sign is
a little crooked.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.416
-Yeah.
-Is that comedy or no?

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.952
-I mean, come on. You tell me.
-Yeah, alright. I think it is.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:56.322
And what was ComedySportz?

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.691
-ComedySportz -- it's this --
I mean, they're still around.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.192
It's a comedy franchise.
-Oh, really?

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:01.360
-Yeah. Where they do, like,
short-form improv,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.361
like "Whose Line Is It Anyway?"

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:03.363
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.396
-And, so, it was in Kansas City.

00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:06.532
And, yeah,
I saw it in high school.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:08.334
It was a place you'd
go to after homecoming,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.570
Because it was a family show,
you weren't allowed to swear.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.272
So when I eventually got to
work on it --

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:14.507
Yeah, if you swore
during a show,

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.476
they would put a
brown paper bag over your head.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.511
They called it
"the brown-bag foul."

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.413
So, you know, they had like --
There was a referee.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.548
You were two teams that are
were, like, red and blue.

00:01:22.548 --> 00:01:23.682
Yeah, it was great.

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:24.783
And you'd "compete"
against each other.

00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:26.052
I mean, you know,
fake competing.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.887
It's kind of like wrestling,
you know, pro wrestling.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.990
You know -- Not to -- Sorry.
Spoilers. Sorry.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.125
I know there's
wrestling fanatics out there

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:34.160
that are like, "No, it's real!"

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.962
It's like, "Alright."
But -- Yeah.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.964
-But that was your first --

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.398
-That was the first foray,
yeah, into, like, doing, like --

00:01:39.398 --> 00:01:40.800
doing improv.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.837
And, yeah, it was -- I mean,
it shaped my life, you know?

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:47.173
And it allowed me to --
You know,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.442
I then went to this high school
called Shawnee Mission West

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.009
and I had this great
teacher named Sally Shipley,

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:53.513
who, a few years before me --
many years before me,

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.748
though you can't tell by looking
at him, Paul Rudd went there.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:59.085
And I go to hand in
homework late one day

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.386
for this radio-and-TV class,

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:02.421
and they're playing these improv
games in the class.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:04.057
I was like, "How the hell
do I take this class?

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.358
You're playing, like,
improv games during school

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:07.860
and you can get
a grade on this?"

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.061
I was like, "Yeah."

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.162
-In Kansas City.
-In Kansas City.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.397
In Overland Park, Kansas, yeah.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.132
And, so, I eventually
did that for, you know,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.568
yeah, like three, four years
before moving to Chicago.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.870
But that was the first,

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.474
you know, go at doing it
and failing at it and all of it.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.075
-Did you do Second City or no?
-Yeah, Second City.

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:24.344
-You did Second City.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.078
-Yeah, Second City,
yeah, moved me up to Chicago

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:28.548
and then did
Second City in Chicago

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:31.050
and then did a thing called
Boom Chicago in Amsterdam,

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.418
then Second City in Las Vegas,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.686
and then eventually
auditioned for "SNL."

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.722
-I met you first on "SNL"
as a writer.

00:02:36.722 --> 00:02:38.091
-My first year, your last year.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.158
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's right.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.493
Yeah, you kind of pushed me out.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.827
-Yeah, yeah.
-I remember that.

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.664
"That's enough."
-And what happened to you since?

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:47.267
-"Jimmy, we've had enough."

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.168
So, dude,
can you tell everyone what --

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:52.038
'Cause this is a story
I've never heard before

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.806
of your audition for
"Saturday Night Live"

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:54.874
at the Comic Strip.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.075
-Yeah, yeah.
No. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.511
Yeah, it was at Stand Up NY.
-Oh, Stand Up NY.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.112
-Yeah, yeah. That's all right.
It's my life.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:01.447
I'm the one that should know.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.117
You got a lot going on.
-Yeah, that's right. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.252
But it's nerve-racking as it is.
-Oh, it's nerve-racking.

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.953
There were 12 dudes.
It was all guys.

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:09.989
Because -- Yeah,
Dean Edwards had just left.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.490
You know, Tracy had just left.
-Okay.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.959
-And so they were
looking for guys.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:15.961
And, so, it was
me and 12 other fellas.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:18.798
I was like fifth or seventh.
I can't quite remember.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.599
And I'm nervous,
as one should be, or excited.

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:22.368
-Do you do stand-up?
-No.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.936
-No.
-No, I did sketch and improv.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:27.739
Like, you know -- So, it
was going up there by yourself.

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:31.677
And I'm standing
there on the sides

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.245
and I drank -- I remember
I was drinking, like,

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:36.849
a Diet Coke and rum, you know,
just to steady my nerves.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.085
I don't -- You know --
-Yeah.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.987
-I was like, "What would
Jimmy Buffett do," right?

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.556
-As one does,
as one should say -- always.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.191
-And they're not going to
make you a margarita

00:03:45.191 --> 00:03:46.492
at a comedy club.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.194
No, the machine's too loud.
So, they do that.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:50.896
And then, all of a sudden,
Jeff Ross comes walking in.

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:52.432
I'm in the lobby, and Jeff Ross,
the roast master general --

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.565
-Comedian, yeah.
-Right.

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:55.134
And I was like, "Oh, wow.
That's Jeff Ross."

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.236
And then, behind him,
in comes walking Chris Rock,

00:03:57.236 --> 00:03:58.537
one of the -- Yeah.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:00.239
So, I'm like, "Oh, okay,
they're probably coming to see

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:01.374
the new talent, the new breed,
what have you.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.475
-Chris was on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.709
-Exactly. Yeah, Chris was there.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:05.144
You know, so -- And when
you're doing this audition

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.412
in this club,
you have the whole --

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.115
Lorne's there and Tina Fey.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.584
Steve Higgins was there
and Mike Shoemaker.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.619
So you have this tribunal
that are in the back,

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.187
and I figured Chris was just
going to join them.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:18.424
Then the person ends, and Chris
is standing right next to me.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.926
-You're about to go up.
-About to go up.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.160
I'd just -- you know...

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.663
You know, suck down my
rum and Diet Coke.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.965
And Chris looks up at me
and he goes, "Oh, hey, man."

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:26.966
I go, "Hey."

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.734
He goes,
"Was this your big shot?"

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.202
I go, "Uh, kinda."

00:04:30.202 --> 00:04:31.337
He goes, "Sorry."

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:32.505
"Ladies and gentlemen,
Chris Rock."

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.074
The guy says that.
The place goes bonkers.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.708
Like, legit bonkers.

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.444
I mean -- No, and I was just --

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.612
And even Lorne was like,
"Ah, it's Chris Rock!"

00:04:40.612 --> 00:04:42.581
-No, he did not.
-No, he did not. He did not.

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:45.317
He did not do that.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.086
-You --
-Yeah. So, he went up.

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.454
Luckily, he only did like
15 minutes.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:51.123
They were preparing jokes
for the MTV Video Music Awards.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.625
-You can't follow Chris Rock.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.526
-"Oh, but you had to, Jason."

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:55.995
No. I know -- you can't.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.530
And, so, he comes down,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.499
and then he walks by me
and he goes, "Hey, man.

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.499
Good luck."

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:02.735
I go, "Thank you.
I appreciate it."

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.036
And he goes,
"They love original thought."

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.371
That was his one little
sentence of advice --

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.672
"They love original thought."

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:08.441
-Chris said that to you
after he just destroyed --

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:09.609
-After he just destroyed
for 20 minutes.

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.377
-Yeah, he's like -- Yeah.
The microphone's melted.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.845
-Exactly. Too hot, too hot.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:13.846
-They love original -- Yeah.

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.180
-Yeah, they love
original thought.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.816
I was like, "I have none.
I have no thoughts right now."

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.518
And, so, then the guy is like,

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:19.585
"Ladies and gentlemen,
Jason Suda-kiss."

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:21.654
And, you know,
said my name wrong.

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:24.523
-Perfect.
-But you know what it felt like?

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.091
It was kind of like
a flag on the play.

00:05:26.091 --> 00:05:29.428
It was like, "Okay, if I bomb,
if I fail right now,

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.731
I'll always be able to sit
at the end of the bar

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.165
in Overland Park, Kansas, going,

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:35.234
"I had to follow
Chris freaking Rock."

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.869
You know, like...
-Exactly.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.805
-Yeah. And, luckily,
it worked out.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.474
I mean, I got hired as a writer,
you know, for a couple years.

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.775
And --
-You worked your way up.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.343
-Yeah, so it was --
It turned out all right.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:45.677
But, yeah,
that was the audition.

00:05:45.677 --> 00:05:49.281
-I can't even tell you --
I heard from so many friends.

00:05:49.281 --> 00:05:51.617
They said, "Have you seen
Jason Sudeikis' show,

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:52.685
'Ted Lasso'?"

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.453
And I go,
"I have not seen this yet."

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:55.822
They go,
"You're going to freak out.

00:05:55.822 --> 00:05:57.990
You're going to cry.
You're going to cry."

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.561
I go -- 'Cause they go, "Yeah,
from comedy, but also emotion.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.162
It's just going to move you.
This one's going to rock you."

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.930
I go, "Let's go. I know Jason."

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.667
I don't know if you --
You've never made me cry before.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.169
-Nope, never have -- on purpose.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:11.937
-Yeah, you made me cry.

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:13.272
-No.
-I love "Ted Lasso."

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:14.607
-Come on.
-Everyone loves "Ted Lasso."

00:06:14.607 --> 00:06:17.043
In fact, we're such giant
"Ted Lasso" fans,

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:18.644
Questlove already
watched Season 2

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:19.845
last night or something.

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:23.549
-Yeah. I did, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:24.883
-He has access to everything.

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:27.053
-Backstage, Quest was trying to
get codes from Jason

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:28.287
to see the rest of the episodes.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:31.991
-Yeah. He goes, "Come on, man."
Asking for codes.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:33.760
Like it's codes.
-I love that.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.494
-"Give me the
golden ticket, Wonka.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:36.929
Come on. Cough it up, buddy."

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.897
-But congrats on this --
20 Emmy nominations.

00:06:38.897 --> 00:06:40.666
You made
television history, buddy.

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:41.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.903
-You made TV history.
-Yeah.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.438
-You knocked it out of the park.

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.939
-Yeah. No, I kicked it
off the pitch,

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:47.973
whatever metaphor works.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:50.309
-Yeah.
-No, I mean, that's lovely.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.378
Luckily, there --
It's an ensemble show,

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:54.413
and so the 20 nominations
go to everybody

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:55.981
that works on the show
in different capacities.

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:57.416
It's a good feeling.
-Well, you worked hard, buddy.

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:59.952
And is there any way to set up
what's going to happen

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.220
in the season or in the last --

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:02.922
-Well, I would say,
yeah, this second season --

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:04.123
This is "Empire Strikes Back."

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:06.492
You know, this --
This starts in the cold

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.260
and it ends in maybe
a little chillier place

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.328
than what we started.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:10.430
-Yeah, okay.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.663
Everybody's got to go
in their cave

00:07:11.663 --> 00:07:14.700
and meet a little green man
and figure it out.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.736
Spoilers, if you haven't seen
"Empire Strikes Back," but...

00:07:16.736 --> 00:07:18.804
-Yeah.
So you're saying Baby Yoda

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.606
might be in
"Ted Lasso" Season 2.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.474
-I mean, you know,
me and Baby Yoda have a history.

00:07:22.474 --> 00:07:24.710
-Okay, alright, yeah.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.978
It's so funny,
and you'll just love it.

00:07:26.978 --> 00:07:28.514
And I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:31.317
Here's Jason Sudeikis in
Season 2 of "Ted Lasso."

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:32.451
Take a look.

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.620
-When Michelle and I
did couples therapy,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.089
it was with this therapist she
had been going to for a while,

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:39.058
and, um...

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:42.161
I just kind of felt like
I was being set up, you know?

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:44.396
Like I was going in there
not to be listened to,

00:07:44.396 --> 00:07:46.631
but rather just to
hear about all the things

00:07:46.631 --> 00:07:47.966
I've been doing wrong.

00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:51.203
-And that's the only time
you've ever seen a therapist?

00:07:51.203 --> 00:07:52.838
-Oh, yeah.
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:54.774
-Do you remember what
you said when I got dumped by

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.308
that cruise-ship dancer
and swore I would never

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:57.776
date another dancer again?

00:07:57.776 --> 00:07:59.178
-"Can I have your tap shoes"?

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:01.813
-"All people
are different people."

00:08:01.813 --> 00:08:04.183
-Mm-hmm. I said that?

00:08:04.183 --> 00:08:05.450
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.886
-Yeah. That's pretty good.

00:08:07.886 --> 00:08:10.222
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah! It is pretty good.

00:08:10.222 --> 00:08:12.959
